Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.4.0
================================================================================
+ Configurable per-connection object ACL with warning for non-public ACLs requiring a CDN URL [#24]
+ Machine-translated language packs for Greek, French, German, Spanish, Italian, and Portuguese [#27]
~ Raised minimum requirements to PHP 8.1 and Joomla 5.4; dropped support for PHP 7.4–8.0 and Joomla 4.x; capped support at PHP 8.6 and Joomla 6.2
# [MEDIUM] Custom region lookup typo (connection['$region'] → connection['custom_region']) broke the "Custom" region option
# [LOW] Dead code in custom endpoint protocol detection (':\' instead of '://'); defaulted to useSSL=true so no working configuration was affected
# [LOW] Escape the Content-Disposition filename in createFile to neutralise quote / backslash / CR / LF
# [LOW] New PathNormaliser strips NUL / CR / LF / '#' / '?' from the configured directory and applies Unicode NFC (ext-intl optional)

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.3.1
================================================================================
# [HIGH] Custom S3-compatible CDN provider ignores the Custom Endpoint URL [#22]

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.3.0
================================================================================
+ EC2 IAM Role authentication
~ PHP 8.5 Compatibility

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.2.2
================================================================================
~ Joomla 6 compatibility: Joomla\CMS\Filesystem has been removed

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.2.1
================================================================================
~ Preliminary support for Joomla 6

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.2.0
================================================================================
- Removed pre-signed URLs
+ Support for third party CDNs with S3-compatible APIs

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.1.4
================================================================================
~ Rewritten bucket validation rule, taking into account Amazon's latest recommendations (January 2025) [#17]

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.1.3
================================================================================
~ PHP 8.4 compatibility: MD5 and SHA-1 functions are deprecated
# [MEDIUM] Amazon S3 no longer allows creating 0-byte files as pseudo-folder entries

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.1.2
================================================================================
# [HIGH] Cannot set up an S3-compatible storage service using v4 signatures

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.1.1
================================================================================
+ Add advanced options for the S3 integration
+ Automatic MIME type detection
# [MEDIUM] Caching was broken
# [MEDIUM] Can't use files with spaces or some special characters in their name
# [LOW] Cannot save third party S3-compatible services' non-compliant access / secret keys

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.1.0
================================================================================
+ Joomla 5 support
~ Using the S3 library through Composer, for easier updates

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.0.2
================================================================================
+ Thumbnails caching on the local filesystem
+ Local caching of Amazon S3 file operations

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.0.1
================================================================================
# [HIGH] Some S3 buckets may return directories with an empty name, breaking Media manager
# [HIGH] Clicking the sidebar folder names leads to an error
# [MEDIUM] No image previews when using straight up S3 (instead of CloudFront)
# [LOW] PHP 8 warning
# [LOW] PHP 8 deprecated notice

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.0.0
